# Smart Phishing URL Detector  
Combining Pattern Analysis, Threat Intelligence, and Domain Profiling for Smarter Phishing Detection

## Project Overview

This project leverages Machine Learning (ML) to detect phishing URLs using two primary data sources:
1. Structural patterns in the URL itself (e.g., length, presence of keywords, special characters)
2. WHOIS domain profiling (e.g., domain age)

The system provides real-time classification of URLs as malicious or benign, along with a risk score and clear explanation for each prediction. It is designed to be lightweight, explainable, and reproducible, making it suitable for both research and practical deployment.

## Features

- Phishing detection using lexical features and domain metadata
- Integration of WHOIS-based domain age analysis
- Real-time `check_url()` prediction function
- Risk score and interpretability (human-readable reasoning)
- Fully implemented in Google Colab with open-source datasets

## Technologies Used

- Python 3.11
- scikit-learn
- pandas
- joblib
- Google Colab

## Dataset Sources

- Malicious URLs Dataset: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/sid321axn/malicious-urls-dataset  
- WHOIS Domain Dataset (100K subset): https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/williamgill/7-million-domains-with-alexa-rank-and-whois

